Method What it gives <code>make()</code> a list of models. They are not saved. <code>makeOne()</code> one model. It is not saved. <code>create()</code> a list of models, saved with <code>save()</code>. <code>createOne()</code> one model, saved with <code>save()</code>. <p><code>count(n)</code> sets how many models <code>make()</code> and <code>create()</code> give. The default is 1.</p> <pre><code>List&lt;User&gt; users = await UserFactory().count(10).create();

User user = UserFactory().makeOne();
</code></pre> <p><code>create()</code> saves the models one by one with <code>save()</code>. So model events run, and each model gets its id.</p>

lib/app/models/blog/blog.model.dart<pre><code>import 'package:dox_orm/dox_orm.dart';

part 'blog.model.g.dart'; // (1)!

@DoxModel() // (2)!
class Blog extends BlogGenerator { // (3)!
  @Column() // (4)!
  String? title;

  @Column(beforeSave: makeSlug) // (5)!
  String? slug;

  @Column()
  String? status;

  @Column(name: 'body') // (6)!
  String? description;

  @Column(name: 'user_id')
  int? userId;

  static String? makeSlug(Map&lt;String, dynamic&gt; map) {
    return map['title']?.toString().toLowerCase().replaceAll(' ', '-');
  }
}
</code></pre> <ol> <li><code>build_runner</code> writes this file. It holds the generated <code>BlogGenerator</code> class.</li> <li>Marks the class as a model. The options, like <code>table</code> and <code>softDelete</code>, go here.     The table is <code>blog</code> by default: the class name in snake_case.</li> <li>The generated class gives the model <code>id</code>, <code>createdAt</code> and <code>updatedAt</code>, and the query builder methods.</li> <li>One <code>@Column()</code> field is one table column. The column name is the field name in snake_case. Digits stay as they are: <code>address2</code> is <code>address2</code>.</li> <li><code>beforeSave</code> runs this static function before a save. It gets all values and returns the value for this column.</li> <li><code>name</code> sets the column name when it is not the snake_case of the field. <code>description</code> reads and writes <code>body</code>. The name is used exactly as written: <code>name: 'userID'</code> is <code>userID</code>.</li> </ol> <p>Make every column field nullable (<code>String?</code>, <code>int?</code>). A new model has no values yet.</p>

