Channel Name Who can subscribe <code>Channel('news')</code> <code>news</code> any client <code>PrivateChannel('orders.5')</code> <code>private-orders.5</code> a client that passes the rule <code>PresenceChannel('chat.lobby')</code> <code>presence-chat.lobby</code> a client that passes the rule. Members see each other <p><code>Broadcast.channel(pattern, rule)</code> adds a rule for private and presence channels. The pattern has no <code>private-</code> or <code>presence-</code> prefix. A <code>{name}</code> part matches any text with no dot. The rule gets the user, then one string for each <code>{name}</code> part. It can be async.</p> <ul> <li>A private rule gives <code>true</code> to allow. Anything else refuses.</li> <li>A presence rule gives a map with the member info, with an <code>id</code>. Anything else refuses.</li> <li>A rule that throws refuses, and the error goes to stderr.</li> </ul> <pre><code>Broadcast.channel('chat.{room}', (Object? user, String room) {
  User u = user as User;
  return &lt;String, Object?&gt;{'id': u.id, 'name': u.name};
});
</code></pre> <p>One rule serves both kinds. <code>orders.{id}</code> checks <code>private-orders.1</code> and <code>presence-orders.1</code>. When more than one pattern matches, the first one added wins.</p>

lib/providers/auth_provider.dart<pre><code>import 'package:dox_auth/dox_auth.dart';
